Int is a whole number, which may be negative
Uint is a whole number that is never negative
Float is a number with a fractional part, rounded
Decimal is an exact amount, such as a price
Text is text
Bytes is raw bytes, such as a stored file
Bool is true or false
Date is a calendar day, with no time on it
Time is a time of day, with no date on it
DateTime is a date and a time, with no time zone
Instant is a moment in time, carrying its own offset
Uuid is a UUID
Json is text the database knows is JSON
Other is anything else, including every array column
Text and Json are the same case: no
